doc2:David Kohan David Sanford Kohan (born April 16, 1964) is an American television producer and writer. After writing for ""The Wonder Years"" and ""The Dennis Miller Show"", Kohan co-created and produced ""Will & Grace"", ""Boston Common"", ""Good Morning, Miami"", ""Twins"" and ""Four Kings"" with Max Mutchnick. Kohan has won an Emmy and a People's Choice Award. He has been nominated for a Golden Globe Award. He and his business partner Max Mutchnick worked on a half-hour comedy series for CBS called ""Partners"". Kohan was born to a Jewish family in New York City and graduated from Wesleyan University in 1986.
