doc0:My Feet Keep Dancing ""My Feet Keep Dancing"" is the third single from Chic's third studio album ""Risqué"". It features a co-lead vocal by Luci Martin and Bernard Edwards and a tap dance solo by Fayard Nicholas (of the Nicholas Brothers), Eugene Jackson (of Our Gang), and Sammy Warren. It reached #21 on the UK pop charts in January 1980, spending 9 weeks on the chart. It failed to enter US Billboard R&B chart Top 40 peaking at #42. On the disco chart, ""My Feet Keep Dancing, along with the cuts, ""Good Times"" and ""My Forbidden Lover"" went to #3
